function t(e,a){return`<BrandProvider brand="${e}" theme="${a}">`}function r(e){return['> Refined hierarchy for TSX generation (React / web). `kind:"component"` = a registered OneUI component from `@jds4/oneui-react` (carries `component`, `props`, `appearance`, `surface`, `text`, `box`, `layout`, `children`). `kind:"surface"` = a surface frame \u2192 `<Surface mode=\u2026>`. `kind:"node"` = structural wrapper \u2192 `<Container>` with the token layout.',"> **Author the screen following the `oneui`, `surface` and `design-composition` skills:**",`> 1. Wrap the screen in \`${e}\` (from \`@jds4/oneui-react\`) and add \`import '@jds4/oneui-react/styles'\` at your entry module.`,'> 2. **Layout = `<Container>`** (token props: `gap="6"`, `paddingX`, `direction`, `justify`, `align`, `columns`\u2026). **Backgrounds = `<Surface mode>`** for any tinted/dark/coloured area \u2014 never a `<div>` with an inline `background`. When a node needs BOTH a tinted background and layout, use `<Container surface="bold" gap="4" \u2026>` (Surface itself is layout-less).',"> 3. **Tokens only** \u2014 role-explicit unified CSS vars (`var(--Body-M-FontSize)`, `var(--Primary-Bold)`, `var(--Text-High)`); never legacy `--Typography-Size-*` / `--Surface-Bold`, never literal px/hex.","> 4. **Images:** ESM-`import` each downloaded asset and pass it as `src` (each Image/Avatar node already has `props.src` set to the downloaded path). No remote Figma URLs.","> **Spacing is token-based:** `layout.gap`/`layout.padding*` are spacing-token KEYS \u2014 emit them as `<Container>` props, never literal px. `layout` also carries `cornerRadius` + `absoluteBox`. Children are already in render order.","> Then run `validate_oneui_code(platform:'react')`. (Tip: re-run with `codegen=true` to auto-generate the .tsx.)"]}function o(e,a){return["## Mode B follow-up prompt","","Use this prompt after the generated scaffold exists:","","```text",`Using the Mode A scaffold written at ${a}, the refined tree returned below, and the assets in assets/figma/,`,"continue authoring the React screen in place.","","Rules:",`- Keep the screen wrapped in ${e} and import UI only from @jds4/oneui-react.`,"- Treat Mode A as the starting scaffold: edit the generated file instead of rebuilding from scratch.","- Use only supported component props from get_component_info/list_components. Do not add raw CSS, CSS variable overrides, hand-drawn replacement DOM, or visual shims just to match a screenshot.","- If fidelity is missing because a component API lacks a prop (for example Slider size, LinearProgressIndicator range offset, or SelectableIconButton default fill), leave the supported component usage visible and note it as a component-level gap.",'- Use <Surface mode="..."> for tinted/dark/coloured regions; do not paint component backgrounds manually.',"- Text variant/size/weight must come from Figma style names where available; use attention for emphasis instead of hardcoded colors.",'- Run validate_oneui_code(platform:"react") after edits.',"- Then run verify_oneui_screen against the generated screen and compare the screenshot to Figma. Iterate only with legitimate OneUI APIs and layout fixes.","```"]}export{r as reactAuthoringGuidance,t as reactProviderTag,o as reactRepairLegacyGuidance};
